# Manually-sourced ML weights (no automatable download URL — see docker/zero-dce/weights/README.md).
# LOL_v2_real.pth (6.2MB) is committed as an exception below: Railway
# builds docker/zero-dce from this git repo (railway.toml uses builder=DOCKERFILE), not from the
# local disk, so a gitignored weight file downloaded locally would never actually reach the deployed
# service — /enhance would keep reporting 503 there even after passing local verification.
# At ~6.2MB this is small enough that committing it (rather than switching to `railway up`
# CLI deploys, or some other transfer mechanism) is the simplest fix. Any OTHER .pth dropped in this
# directory in the future still defaults to gitignored, per the general rule below.
# (dehazeformer-t.pth was a previous exception here — removed 2026-08-27 along with DehazeFormer-T
# itself, see docs/SPEC.md's rejected-models section.)
docker/zero-dce/weights/*.pth
!docker/zero-dce/weights/LOL_v2_real.pth

# Python bytecode cache (produced by local py_compile/server runs while testing docker/zero-dce)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

